    "rationale": "The proposed “bản xem trước phóng đại” repairs the current unnatural word stack, but “khi vẽ” introduces an avoidable temporal reading (“while drawing”) absent from the English. This same checkbox controls cursorMagnifier as well as activeMagnifier. In current static source, magnifierVisible accepts supportsCursor() without requiring down or cursorDrawing, so the lens can describe the cursor position before an active stroke. “Hiện bản xem trước phóng đại của bản vẽ” preserves the preview as the object and the drawing as its content, without suggesting a stroke-only visibility condition. This is a clarity precaution rather than a claim that every reader must misread the proposed wording.",
